          question: 'What is the ACSC Essential Eight and does ClickMasters implement it?',
          answer: 'The ACSC (Australian Cyber Security Centre) Essential Eight is a set of eight baseline mitigation strategies that the Australian government recommends for all Australian organisations to protect against cyber threats. The eight strategies: application control (only approved applications can execute), patching applications (within 48 hours of critical patches), configuring Microsoft Office macros (disable macros from the internet), user application hardening (disable Flash, ads, Java in browsers), restricting administrative privileges (limited to those who need it), patching operating systems (within 48 hours of critical patches), multi-factor authentication (for all users, especially privileged accounts and remote access), and regular backups (tested, isolated from the network, covering all critical data). The Australian government mandates Essential Eight compliance for all federal government systems at a minimum of Maturity Level 2. APRA-regulated financial institutions are strongly recommended to achieve Essential Eight compliance. ClickMasters implements Essential Eight controls and documents them against the ACSC\'s Maturity Level framework as part of Australian enterprise security engagements.',
